# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Git already stores every text file here with LF. Without this file, a Windows
# checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` gets CRLF on disk instead, and Biome — which
# formats to LF — then reports every file in the repo as unformatted. CI, running
# on Linux, sees none of it. Pinning `eol=lf` keeps the two honest: what a
# contributor formats is what CI checks, on any platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

